# Array of structures: initialiser, indexed member access, copy semantics.
#
# Derivation (ed.3 6.4.4.4.2 and table 14 (structure initialiser
# "(x := 1, y := 10)" inside an array initialiser); 6.4.4.4 program
# variables keep their value between cycles; assignment of a structure
# copies it):
#   pts starts as (1,10) (2,20) (3,30); pts[2].x accumulates k.
#   sum_y is always 60 and copy_y always 30 (c.y := c.y + 1 touches the
#   copy only).
# cycle 0: k=1  -> pts[2].x = 3:  sum_x = 1+3+3 = 7,  px = 3
# cycle 1: k=0  -> still 3:        sum_x = 7,          px = 3
# cycle 2: k=5  -> 8:              sum_x = 12,         px = 8
# cycle 3: k=-8 -> 0:              sum_x = 4,          px = 0
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: k
outputs: sum_x sum_y px copy_y
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 6.4.4.4.2 (initialisation), table 14 (array of structures); ed.2 2.4.3.1
---
0 k=1 => sum_x=7 sum_y=60 px=3 copy_y=30
1 k=0 => sum_x=7 sum_y=60 px=3 copy_y=30
2 k=5 => sum_x=12 sum_y=60 px=8 copy_y=30
3 k=-8 => sum_x=4 sum_y=60 px=0 copy_y=30
